{
  "requirement": "`LanguageId` is a public struct with a private string. Construct one from `&str`\nor `String`, for example `LanguageId::from(\"rust\")`. `as_str()` borrows the\noriginal name. Serde represents the identifier as a string.\n\n`StructuralQuery::language` takes a `LanguageId`. Construction preserves the\nspelling. Structural search looks up the name among the configured languages\nand returns an error for an unknown name.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct LanguageId(/* private fields */);\n\nimpl LanguageId {\n    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for LanguageId;\nimpl Debug for LanguageId;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for LanguageId;\nimpl From<&str> for LanguageId;\nimpl From<String> for LanguageId;\nimpl Hash for LanguageId;\nimpl PartialEq for LanguageId;\nimpl Serialize for LanguageId;\nimpl Eq for LanguageId;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.language_id`.\n\n**Construction and `as_str()`**\n- `source_bytes_error_kinds_and_language_names_round_trip` builds `LanguageId::from(\"CustomLang\")`.\n- It asserts that `as_str()` returns exactly `\"CustomLang\"`, so mixed-case spelling is preserved.\n- It asserts that `LanguageId::from(String::from(\"CustomLang\"))` equals the `&str`-built value. That covers both `From` impls and `PartialEq`/`Eq`.\n\n**Serde as a string**\n- The same test asserts `serde_json::to_value(&name)` equals the JSON string `\"CustomLang\"`.\n- It then deserializes that value and asserts it equals the original, so both `Serialize` and `Deserialize` are covered.\n\n**`StructuralQuery::language` takes a `LanguageId`**\n- `StructuralQuery::new(name, ...)` is exercised with `LanguageId` values.\n- `built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope` also builds queries with `\"rust\".into()` and `\"python\".into()`. It asserts that structural search finds matches in the matching language only: `visible.rs` for rust, and `script.py` for python.\n- That covers the lookup among configured languages.\n\n**Unknown name**\n- The first test runs `search_structure` on a query for the unconfigured `CustomLang`. It asserts `Err(SourceError::Invalid(message))` where the message contains `\"CustomLang\"`. That checks both the error and that the spelling is preserved through construction.\n\n**Trait impls**\n- `Clone` is used in both tests.\n- `Debug` and `Hash` are listed in the requirement but are derive-only, with no conditional or transformation of their own. They fall under the no-logic exemption.\n- `public_exports_match_the_appendix` checks the public export inventory.\n\n**Private field**\n- This is enforced by the type definition itself (`pub struct LanguageId(String)`), and the tests only use public APIs.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "3c2a02796d0ce8a489570e43492c83c3123514508b0835799933c75335ff0a73",
